      "id": 1,
      "text": "Richland began as a depot town when the Houston and Texas Central Railway built a station on Pisgah Ridge in 1871.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richland%2C_Texas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the mid‑1890s Richland boasted two steam gristmills, cotton gins, three general stores, a bank, and a population of about 150.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richland%2C_Texas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s first school operated during the Civil War, and by 1906 it had a two‑teacher classroom with seventy‑five students.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
